{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UnitalGroebnerBasesChapter.DivisionAlgorithm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UnitalGroebnerBasesChapter.DivisionAlgorithm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.division_algorithm_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.division_algorithm_exists","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/division-algorithm.lean#L38-L55","doc":"The division algorithm terminates and produces a decomposition\n`f = nf + remainder` where `nf` is a normal form (irreducible\nunder the generators) and `remainder` lies in the ideal generated\nby the leading terms.\n\nExistence of normal forms is axiomatized (Bergman 1978, Theorem 1.2);\nthe reduction function and correctness theorems are proved in\n`folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.InIdeal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.InIdeal","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/division-algorithm.lean#L33-L36","doc":"Ideal membership: `remainder` is in the two-sided ideal\ngenerated by `generators`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.IsNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.IsNormalForm","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/division-algorithm.lean#L27-L31","doc":"A normal form predicate: `r` is irreducible with respect to\nthe leading terms of `generators`.  Axiomatized here; the full\ndefinition is `QOU.GrobnerShirshov.IsNormalForm` in Basic.lean. ","signatureChunk":0}]}